# BotMaker line endings — docs/refactor/00-conventions.md §4.
#
# Byte-identical in all seven repos. This exists because the tree is genuinely edited from two
# platforms (release.ps1 and testing/windows/ are Windows-toolchain artefacts), and without it the
# working-tree line ending of a file depends on whoever last touched it and how their core.autocrlf
# was set. `text=auto eol=lf` normalises everything to LF in the object store; the two exceptions
# below are the files a Windows shell actually executes.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Generated by Gradle; leave its bytes alone.
gradlew.bat -text

# Binary, so git never tries to normalise or diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
